WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.075
Part 2: divisions under
central governance.

2
00:00:03.075 --> 00:00:06.300
Module 3 covers divisions on NIOS.

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.425
Most agencies aren't one network.

4
00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:13.429
Bureaus, regional offices and labs run
their own address space and often their own

5
00:00:13.429 --> 00:00:17.845
DNS, and a central policy plane only
works if those divisions can still do

6
00:00:17.845 --> 00:00:22.113
their jobs through it, because a
division that can't will work around it.

7
00:00:22.113 --> 00:00:25.626
NIOS has a detailed permission
model for exactly this.

8
00:00:25.626 --> 00:00:30.750
We'll go through how it decides access, how
to scope an admin group to one division,

9
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:36.031
the views and attributes that separate
divisions, approvals and their one big gap,

10
00:00:36.031 --> 00:00:40.613
sign-in, Microsoft servers, what stays
central, and a reporting surprise.

11
00:00:40.613 --> 00:00:46.000
Sources: Infoblox NIOS 9.1.x
and 9.0 administration guides;

12
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.460
the Federal Modernization
Workbook's Book 08, Chapter 11.
